From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:58:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebCommon+LibWebView+WebDriver: Add WebAuthn
 virtual authenticators

This adds the virtual authenticators of WebAuthn's WebDriver extension:
software CTAP1/U2F and CTAP2 authenticators with P-256 credentials,
discoverable credentials and user verification on demand, which the UI
process's ceremonies find as they would security keys. WebDriver gets
the extension's commands to add and remove them, add, list and remove
their credentials, and set whether the user is verified. With a virtual
authenticator present, a tab's ceremonies run without asking anyone, as
under automation nobody is there to answer.

Tests reach the same commands through Internals, and testdriver-vendor.js
uses them for WPT's add_virtual_authenticator() and its relatives. A
test's virtual authenticators belong to its own tab, since test-web runs
tests side by side in one browser process.

The new tests register a credential and sign in with it, checking the
assertion's signature with WebCrypto, run a ceremony in a cross-origin
iframe with and without allow="publickey-credentials-get", check the
argument errors, and drive the WebDriver extension end to end. Eight of
WPT's webauthn tests are imported, and all of their subtests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
